steps.reasoning_content:
Now I have the full picture. Key constraints and plan:

**Constraints discovered:**
- `react-big-calendar@1.20.0` is locked (installed via npm ci). Localizer date libs bundled as deps: dayjs, moment, moment-timezone, luxon, globalize, date-arithmetic → use `dayjsLocalizer` (dayjs will be in node_modules as transitive dep). Actually wait — importing `dayjs` directly in client code relies on hoisting. npm workspaces hoists to root `node_modules`. Vite resolves from there fine. TypeScript `moduleResolution: bundler` resolves node_modules fine. dayjs has bundled types. OK.
  - Alternatively use `momentLocalizer`. dayjs is cleaner. I'll use dayjs.
- `react-dnd` NOT in lockfile → official `withDragAndDrop` addon unusable without new deps (forbidden). → Custom HTML5 DnD implementation for move + resize in month view.
- No shadcn/ui components installed (no components/ui dir) → hand-rolled Tailwind modals, matching Login page style.
- Server: prisma is mocked in tests (vi.mock('@/lib/prisma')). Events routes must use `prisma.event` so tests can mock it.
- `noUnusedLocals`, `noUnusedParameters` strict — careful.
- eslint: @typescript-eslint/recommended — no `any` warnings? `@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any` is 'warn' in recommended → max-warnings 0 fails lint on `any`. Avoid `any`.

**Server implementation:**

`server/src/services/event.ts`:
```ts
import { prisma } from '@/lib/prisma'
import type { Event } from '@prisma/client'

export interface EventRange { start?: Date; end?: Date }
export interface CreateEventInput { title: string; description?: string | null; start: Date; end: Date }
export interface UpdateEventInput { title?: string; description?: string | null; start?: Date; end?: Date }

export async function listEvents(userId: string, range: EventRange): Promise<Event[]>
// overlap filter: start < range.end && end > range.start
export async function createEvent(userId: string, input: CreateEventInput): Promise<Event>
export async function findOwnedEvent(userId: string, id: string): Promise<Event | null>  // findFirst({userId,id})
export async function updateEvent(userId, id, input): Promise<Event | null>
export async function deleteEvent(userId, id): Promise<boolean>
```

`server/src/routes/events.ts`:
```ts
const dateSchema = z.coerce.date()
const createEventSchema = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(1).max(200),
  description: z.string().max(5000).nullish(),  // hmm keep simple: optional
  start: dateSchema, end: dateSchema,
}).refine(d => d.start < d.end, '종료 시각은 시작 시각보다 뒤여야 합니다.')

const updateEventSchema = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(1).max(200).optional(),
  description: z.string().max(5000).nullable().optional(),
  start: dateSchema.optional(),
  end: dateSchema.optional(),
})
// PUT: merge with existing then check start<end
```

Routes mounted with `requireAuth` on all: `router.use(requireAuth)`.

- GET `/` : parse `start`/`end` query params — `z.coerce.date().optional()` — invalid → 400.
- POST `/` : 400 on parse fail; 201 `{ event }`.
- PUT `/:id` : find owned event → 404 if not; parse body → 400; merge start/end for validate → 400 if start>=end; update → `{ event }`.
- DELETE `/:id` : owned? → 404 else delete → `{ ok: true }` or 204. I'll use `{ ok: true }` consistent with logout style.

Wait — description nullable handling: Prisma `description String?` — null means clear. For PUT, `description: null` clears it. Zod: `z.string().max(2000).nullish()` allows undefined (don't touch) and null (clear). For create, `nullish` → store as null.

`app.ts`: `import eventRoutes from '@/routes/events'` and `app.use('/api/events', eventRoutes)`.

**Client implementation:**

`client/src/types/schemas.ts` — add:
```ts
export const eventSchema = z.object({
  id: z.string(),
  title: z.string(),
  description: z.string().nullable(),
  start: z.string(),  // ISO
  end: z.string(),
})
export type CalendarEvent = z.infer<typeof eventSchema>

export const eventInputSchema = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(1, '제목을 입력하세요.').max(200, ...),
  description: z.string().max(2000).optional(),
  start: z.string().min(1, '시작 시각을 입력하세요.'),
  end: z.string().min(1, '종료 시각을 입력하세요.'),
}).refine(d => new Date(d.start) < new Date(d.end), { message: '종료 시각은 시작 시각보다 뒤여야 합니다.', path: ['end'] })
export type EventInput = z.infer<typeof eventInputSchema>
```

Client uses `datetime-local` inputs → produce local ISO; send ISO strings via `new Date(value).toISOString()`.

`client/src/api/events.ts`:
```ts
export function useEvents(range?: { start?: string; end?: string }) {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: ['events', range],
    queryFn: async () => {
      const { data } = await api.get<{ events: CalendarEvent[] }>('/events', { params: range })
      return data.events
    },
  })
}
export function useCreateEvent() → POST /events, invalidate ['events']
export function useUpdateEvent() → PUT /events/:id ({id, input}), invalidate
export function useDeleteEvent() → DELETE, invalidate
```

`client/src/pages/Calendar.tsx`:
- `Calendar` from 'react-big-calendar' with `dayjsLocalizer(dayjs)`, `views={['month']}` (월간 뷰), `localizer`, `events` mapped to `{...ev, start: new Date(ev.start), end: new Date(ev.end)}`, `selectable`, `onSelectSlot` → open create modal, `onSelectEvent` → open detail modal.
- Custom DnD:
  - `components.event` → custom `DraggableEvent` div: `draggable`, `onDragStart` sets drag payload {eventId, mode} into a ref/context + dataTransfer. Includes left/right edge handles: two child divs positioned at edges with `cursor: ew-resize`; their `onDragStart` sets mode 'resize-start'/'resize-end' and stops propagation.
  - `components.dateCellWrapper` → custom wrapper: clone children with added `onDragOver` (preventDefault → allow drop), `onDrop` → compute target date from `value` prop passed to dateCellWrapper children (rbc passes `value` to DateCellWrapper). Then:
    - move: shift event so that `start` date becomes target date keeping time-of-day; keep duration. Actually simpler: keep duration, set start = target date at original start time-of-day, end = start + duration.
    - resize-end: end = end-of-day of target date (or target date with original end time). Validate start<end.
    - resize-start: start = start-of-day of target (or original time). Validate.
  - On drop → `updateEvent.mutate` → 서버 자동 저장.

Where to put the drag payload state? `dateCellWrapper` and `event` components need shared context. Options:
  1. Module-level mutable ref in Calendar.tsx file (a plain exported internal variable) — works since single calendar instance.
  2. dataTransfer.setData('text/plain', JSON.stringify(payload)) — jsdom may not fully support dataTransfer but tests will test pure helpers anyway.
  Use both: dataTransfer for real DnD + a module-level `dragState` fallback? Simpler: use a module-level variable (also used as source of truth); dataTransfer needed to satisfy browser drag protocol — actually for HTML5 DnD, you need `event.dataTransfer.setData(...)` in dragstart for Firefox to allow drag, and `dragover` preventDefault for drop to fire. I'll set data AND module ref.

  Pure helper functions for testability in `client/src/lib/event-dnd.ts`:
  ```ts
  export type DragMode = 'move' | 'resize-start' | 'resize-end'
  export function applyMove(start: Date, end: Date, target: Date): {start,end}
  export function applyResizeEnd(start: Date, end: Date, target: Date): {start,end} | null  // null if invalid
  export function applyResizeStart(...): | null
  ```

- Modals: `EventFormModal` (create/edit: title, description, start, end with datetime-local), `ConfirmDeleteModal`. Delete flow: click event → detail/edit modal with "삭제" button → opens confirm modal → confirm → deleteEvent.mutate.
- `App.tsx`: add route `/calendar` → `<ProtectedRoute><Calendar/></ProtectedRoute>`.

Also need `import 'react-big-calendar/lib/css/react-big-calendar.css'` in Calendar.tsx.

For rbc styling to look reasonable with Tailwind tokens — minimal custom CSS in index.css? Not required. Keep it simple: add a few CSS rules via index.css `.rbc-calendar` overrides? I'll skip heavy styling; maybe add `height` via style prop `style={{ height: 700 }}`.

